research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field.log-3499-  an ordered field, and the point of the page they open is that in the presence
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field.log:3500:  of (ARCH) they are all the same predicate ([[thm-completeness-equivalences]]),
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field.log-3501-  while without it two of them are strictly weaker
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-ex-cauchy-complete-not-complete-field.log-3502-  ([[fs-nested-intervals-implies-lub]], [[fs-cauchy-complete-implies-lub]]).
