research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20538-['lem-cauchy-complete-and-archimedean-imply-mct','ai-altered',P,'semantic-source',[C],'Hall states the equivalence of sequential Cauchy and monotone completeness in Archimedean ordered fields. The local theorem exposes ARCH and supplies a dependency-adapted increment argument.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20539-['lem-mct-implies-archimedean','ai-altered',P,'semantic-source',[C],'Hall defines monotone completeness in the ordered-field setting and places it in the Archimedean completeness equivalence. The local item isolates the standard canonical-naturals contradiction showing MCT forces ARCH.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20540-['lem-mct-implies-lub','ai-altered',P,'semantic-source',[C],'Hall states monotone and Dedekind completeness as equivalent for Archimedean ordered fields. The local statement keeps an explicitly redundant ARCH hypothesis and constructs the supremum by bisection.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log:20541:['thm-completeness-equivalences','ai-altered',P,'semantic-source',[C],'Hall Theorem 3.11 gives equivalence of Dedekind, monotone, Cantor, Bolzano-Weierstrass, and sequential completeness for Archimedean ordered fields. The local theorem repackages exactly the five selected clauses so ARCH is attached only to NIP and CC.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20542-['def-cesaro-mean','literature-derived',N,'exact-source',[ES],'The Encyclopedia of Mathematics defines the arithmetic averages (s_0+...+s_n)/(n+1) and summability by their limit. This matches the local zero-based definition and direction.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20543-['thm-cesaro-mean-theorem','literature-derived',P,'exact-source',[ES],'The source states Cauchy’s theorem that s_n tending to s implies its arithmetic averages tend to s, with the same quantifiers and conclusion. The numbered head-tail proof is local.'],
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-20544-['thm-stolz-cesaro','ai-altered',P,'semantic-source',[U.stolz],'The source gives the infinity-over-infinity Stolz-Cesaro theorem for a strictly increasing unbounded denominator and convergent difference quotient. The local version changes indexing and states the conclusion on a positive tail to admit b_0=0.'],
