research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-32231-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-32232-[L4] $K$ is not Archimedean, since $n \cdot 1_K < t$ for every natural $n$ ([[lem-laurent-non-archimedean]], [[def-archimedean-field]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log-32233-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits.log:32234:[L5] For an ordered field, the Archimedean property together with (NIP) does imply (LUB) ([[thm-completeness-equivalences]], clause 2 implies clause 1).
