research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8946-**False claim:** every ordered field with the nested interval property (NIP) of
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8947-[[def-completeness-properties]] has the least-upper-bound property (LUB).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8948-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log:8949:This is clause 2 of [[thm-completeness-equivalences]] with its Archimedean
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8950-hypothesis deleted, and the deletion is exactly what makes it false. The witness
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8951-is the formal Laurent series field $K = \mathbb{R}((t^{-1}))$, which satisfies
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-8952-(NIP) and has no least upper bound for the set of its own canonical naturals.
