research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19423--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19424--- **The companion failure** is [[fs-cauchy-complete-implies-lub]], refuted by the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19425--  same field. Together they are the exact content of the Archimedean hypotheses
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log:19426:-  in clauses 2 and 4 of [[thm-completeness-equivalences]].
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19427-+- **The failure is not an accident of one field.** By [[lem-lub-implies-nested-intervals]] every field with (LUB) is Archimedean, so any witness at all must be non-Archimedean; and in a non-Archimedean field the shrinking hypothesis in (NIP) is a severe restriction, because a length that tends to $0$ in the order of the field must get below every infinitesimal. That is why $K$ satisfies the shrinking form while failing the unrestricted one, and it is why $K$ can satisfy (NIP) while failing (LUB) at all.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19428-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19429-+- **$\mathbb{R}(t)$ will not do as a witness**, although it is the library's other non-Archimedean ordered field ([[cex-ordered-field-not-archimedean]]). Nothing in this library establishes any nested interval property for it, and the page that built $K$ says why a new field was constructed rather than reusing that one.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log-19430-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-completeness-limits-apply.log:19431:+- **The companion failure** is [[fs-cauchy-complete-implies-lub]], refuted by the same field. Together they are the exact content of the Archimedean hypotheses in clauses 2 and 4 of [[thm-completeness-equivalences]].
